Z||000002||Fleabitdog||07-12-2001||09:49 AM||||Haggster.  That happened to me about six years ago in Phoenixville, Pa. My fine was about the same amount. I paid it and just did not cruise in Phoenixville anymore. What sucks is the tints were in the legal degrees of tint for Pa. but it was aftermarket. Stupid, stupid law.||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||07-12-2001||09:50 AM||||theres supposed to be a solution to take the glue off at parts store, i never used it, but worth a try. just use a razor to get a corner loose and peel it off. if you go slow lots of times itll come off with the glue and not leave much of anything. Ive used alcohol, and windex WITH AMMONIA, or a mixture of ammonia and water. then scraped it with a single edge razor blade. clean up whats left with OOO steelwool <P>(isnt it strange with all the crime around, that cops have nothing else to do but this trival crap)<BR>||||reg||1
