Z||000014||DecadenceR||07-13-2001||03:25 PM||||In jersey you can't have anything on your front windshiled that's doesn't allow light to pass, and it can't be further than 6 inches down drom the top. Side wintows, you can' thave anything. Rear windows there's no law against anything. But you're not allowed reflective (mirrored) tint. however, most SUVs come with that standard. So, is that still illegal?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>On my old Eclipse I had 5% all the way around except the windshield. I never got bothered in my town, or where I was dating this girl. But when I went to work the next town north, I got stopped EVERY time. Thanksfully I was dating a sheriff's daughter, so I had a steady supply of PBA cards at the time.||||reg||1
