Z||000016||MoneypitGT||07-13-2001||10:11 PM||||F-That, pay the $93.50, which is what it should be, and have a nice day officer. The law is a joke and the only way to get around it is if they used a tint meter. The use of a tint meter is illegal search and seizure of your car and is dismissed in court. I know, been there many times and all my cars are tinted heavily (good friend of a tint shop), most of the cops don't even care anymore, because they know it isn't coming off. <BR>Chris<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.customdynamix.com/images/blackrear.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR><B>Check out my site at:</B>   <A HREF="http://www.customdynamix.com" TARGET=_blank>www.customdynamix.com</A> <BR>2 '87 GT Projects||||reg||1
Z||000017||johnt671||07-15-2001||09:34 AM||||I got stopped a few years ago for the same thing.  I was on my way to work and the cop hung a uey to stop me.  Want to know were I bought the car as I just moved here from N.Y. Then he wanted to to know where I was going.  Work, I told him.  Where did I work he wanted to know.  None of your business I replied, so he gave me ticket and told me to remove it.  Later that day I saw a ricer Ford Escort that had the windos so dark he had cut some the layers off by his side mirrors so he could see out them.  He rode around that way for three years.||||reg||1
